IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wcin-common`
IMPORT `wcin-dates`
IMPORT `wcin-wirc-2013`
IMPORT `wcin-aca-1985`

-- Victorian workers' compensation indexation notice, Gazette S 363 of 30 June 2026 -- the questions of the dependants and
-- close family members of a worker who dies, and of the family of a worker severely injured.
--
-- SEAT: the dependent partner, the dependent child (or whoever asks for the child), another dependant, and a close or
-- non-dependent family member of a worker who dies at work; and, for the hospital travel row, a family member of a
-- severely injured worker. "How much is my share of the lump sum? What is the most other dependants can get? What is the
-- most my weekly pension can be, and what does the notice print for its calculation? What can I be paid for grief, for
-- expenses, for travel to the funeral? What does the notice set for damages for the death?" Whether a person is a
-- dependant, a partner, an orphan or a close family member is decided under the Act (not deposited): each is asked as a
-- fact. The rules are in wcin-wirc-2013.l4 and wcin-aca-1985.l4; this module restates none. Its names differ from
-- wcin-seat.l4's, so a case file can import both.
--
-- WHICH DAY. Every question asks for a day from 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027 and uses the column in force on it; any other
-- day answers `not covered`. Which day counts for a death benefit (the day of death, of the claim, of payment) is the
-- Act's.
--
