§ `Victorian workers' compensation amounts from 1 July 2026 -- the family of a worker who dies`

§§ `The lump sum for the worker's death (2013 Act ss 236, 237; 1985 Act s 92A)`

@export How much is my share of the lump sum paid for the death of a worker in Victoria, as the notice's shares state it?
GIVEN `the Act the death claim is under` IS A `Governing Act` @desc Which Act the claim for the worker's death is under: the Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013, or, for an older claim, the Accident Compensation Act 1985
      `the day we ask about` IS A DATE @desc The day for which you want the amount (the Act decides which day counts, such as the day of death); from 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027
      `I am` IS A `Dependant kind` @desc Whether you are a dependent partner of the worker, or a dependent child (or asking for one)
      `how many dependent partners the worker left` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dependent partners the worker left (0 if none); partially dependent partners are not counted
      `how many dependent children the worker left` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dependent children the worker left (0 if none)
      `the dependent children are orphans` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the dependent children are orphans; used only where the worker left no dependent partner
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`my share of the death lump sum` `the Act the death claim is under` `the day we ask about` `I am` `how many dependent partners the worker left` `how many dependent children the worker left` `the dependent children are orphans` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the notice column in force on` `the day we ask about`
    WHEN `not covered` `the gap` THEN `not covered` `the gap`
    WHEN `answered` `the column` THEN
        CONSIDER `the Act the death claim is under`
        WHEN `the Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013` THEN
            `the 2013 Act share of the death lump sum of` `I am` `with partners` `how many dependent partners the worker left` `children` `how many dependent children the worker left` `orphans` `the dependent children are orphans` `in` `the column`
        WHEN `the Accident Compensation Act 1985` THEN
            `the 1985 Act share of the death lump sum of` `I am` `with partners` `how many dependent partners the worker left` `children` `how many dependent children the worker left` `orphans` `the dependent children are orphans` `in` `the column`

@export What is the most the lump sum can be for the dependent children, dependent partners and partially dependent partners of a worker who dies (2013 Act s 237(1); 1985 Act s 92A(8B))?
GIVEN `the Act the death claim is under` IS A `Governing Act` @desc Which Act the claim for the worker's death is under
      `the day we ask about` IS A DATE @desc The day for which you want the amount; from 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`the most the lump sum can be for partners and children` `the Act the death claim is under` `the day we ask about` MEANS
    `the figure under` `the Act the death claim is under` `on` `the day we ask about` `from` (JUST `the 2013 Act s 237(1) maximum`) `or` (JUST `the 1985 Act s 92A(8B) maximum`)

@export What is the most the lump sum can be for dependent children where the worker left no dependent partner (2013 Act s 236(6); 1985 Act s 92A(8A))?
GIVEN `the Act the death claim is under` IS A `Governing Act` @desc Which Act the claim for the worker's death is under
      `the day we ask about` IS A DATE @desc The day for which you want the amount; from 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`the most the lump sum can be for children with no dependent partner` `the Act the death claim is under` `the day we ask about` MEANS
    `the figure under` `the Act the death claim is under` `on` `the day we ask about` `from` (JUST `the 2013 Act s 236(6) maximum`) `or` (JUST `the 1985 Act s 92A(8A) maximum`)

@export What is the most other dependants can be paid as a lump sum where the worker left no dependent partner, dependent child or partially dependent partner (2013 Act s 237(2); 1985 Act s 92A(9))?
GIVEN `the Act the death claim is under` IS A `Governing Act` @desc Which Act the claim for the worker's death is under
      `the day we ask about` IS A DATE @desc The day for which you want the amount; from 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`the most other dependants can be paid where no partner or child is left` `the Act the death claim is under` `the day we ask about` MEANS
    `the figure under` `the Act the death claim is under` `on` `the day we ask about` `from` (JUST `the 2013 Act s 237(2) maximum`) `or` (JUST `the 1985 Act s 92A(9) maximum`)

@export What is the most other dependants can be paid as a lump sum under the row for other dependants (2013 Act s 237AA(1); 1985 Act s 92A(8C))?
GIVEN `the Act the death claim is under` IS A `Governing Act` @desc Which Act the claim for the worker's death is under
      `the day we ask about` IS A DATE @desc The day for which you want the amount; from 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`the most other dependants can be paid under the other dependants row` `the Act the death claim is under` `the day we ask about` MEANS
    `the figure under` `the Act the death claim is under` `on` `the day we ask about` `from` (JUST `the 2013 Act s 237AA(1) maximum`) `or` (JUST `the 1985 Act s 92A(8C) maximum`)

@export What compensation does the notice set for a close family member's grief or loss on a worker's death (2013 Act s 237A(1); 1985 Act s 92A(11A))?
GIVEN `the Act the death claim is under` IS A `Governing Act` @desc Which Act the claim for the worker's death is under
      `the day we ask about` IS A DATE @desc The day for which you want the amount; from 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`the grief or loss compensation for a close family member` `the Act the death claim is under` `the day we ask about` MEANS
    `the figure under` `the Act the death claim is under` `on` `the day we ask about` `from` (JUST `the 2013 Act s 237A(1) amount`) `or` (JUST `the 1985 Act s 92A(11A) amount`)

@export What is the most I can be reimbursed for expenses as a family member who was not a dependant of the worker (2013 Act s 240(9); 1985 Act s 92AA)?
GIVEN `the Act the death claim is under` IS A `Governing Act` @desc Which Act the claim for the worker's death is under
      `the day we ask about` IS A DATE @desc The day for which you want the amount; from 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`the most a non-dependent family member can be reimbursed` `the Act the death claim is under` `the day we ask about` MEANS
    `the figure under` `the Act the death claim is under` `on` `the day we ask about` `from` (JUST `the 2013 Act s 240(9) maximum`) `or` (JUST `the 1985 Act s 92AA maximum`)

§§ `Weekly pensions for dependants (2013 Act s 241; 1985 Act s 92B)`

@export What is the most I can be paid as a weekly pension as a dependant of a worker who died (my equal share of the notice's maximum)?
GIVEN `the Act the death claim is under` IS A `Governing Act` @desc Which Act the claim for the worker's death is under
      `the week we ask about` IS A DATE @desc A day in the week for which you want the pension figure; from 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027
      `the day the claim was made` IS A DATE @desc The day the claim was made; used only for a 1985 Act claim, whose rows differ before and from 5 April 2010
      `I am` IS A `Dependant kind` @desc Whether you are a dependent partner, or a dependent child (or asking for one)
      `how many dependent partners the worker left` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dependent partners the worker left (0 if none)
      `the dependent children are orphans` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the dependent children are orphans; used only where the worker left no dependent partner
      `how many dependent children are entitled to a pension` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dependent children are entitled to a pension
      `the pension period` IS A `Pension period` @desc Whether the week is during the first 13 weeks, after them but before the end of three years, or after the end of three years (as the Act counts them)
GIVETH AN `Answer` `Pension figure`
`the most my weekly pension can be` `the Act the death claim is under` `the week we ask about` `the day the claim was made` `I am` `how many dependent partners the worker left` `the dependent children are orphans` `how many dependent children are entitled to a pension` `the pension period` MEANS
    `the pension figure for` `the maximum row` `in` (`the notice column in force on` `the week we ask about`)
    WHERE
        `the maximum row` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the Act the death claim is under`
            WHEN `the Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013` THEN
                `the 2013 Act maximum weekly pension row for` `I am` `with partners` `how many dependent partners the worker left` `orphans` `the dependent children are orphans` `children` `how many dependent children are entitled to a pension` `during` `the pension period`
            WHEN `the Accident Compensation Act 1985` THEN
                `the 1985 Act maximum weekly pension row for` `I am` `with partners` `how many dependent partners the worker left` `orphans` `the dependent children are orphans` `children` `how many dependent children are entitled to a pension` `during` `the pension period` `claim before 5 April 2010` (`the claim was made before 5 April 2010` `the day the claim was made`)

@export What amount does the notice print for the Act's weekly pension calculation for me as a dependant of a worker who died?
GIVEN `the Act the death claim is under` IS A `Governing Act` @desc Which Act the claim for the worker's death is under
      `the week we ask about` IS A DATE @desc A day in the week for which you want the figure; from 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027
      `the day the claim was made` IS A DATE @desc The day the claim was made; used only for a 1985 Act claim
      `I am` IS A `Dependant kind` @desc Whether you are a dependent partner, or a dependent child (or asking for one)
      `how many dependent partners the worker left` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dependent partners the worker left (0 if none)
      `how many dependent children are entitled to a pension` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dependent children are entitled to a pension
      `the pension period` IS A `Pension period` @desc Whether the week is during the first 13 weeks, after them but before the end of three years, or after the end of three years
GIVETH AN `Answer` `Pension figure`
`the amount the notice prints for my pension calculation` `the Act the death claim is under` `the week we ask about` `the day the claim was made` `I am` `how many dependent partners the worker left` `how many dependent children are entitled to a pension` `the pension period` MEANS
    `the pension figure for` `the calculation row` `in` (`the notice column in force on` `the week we ask about`)
    WHERE
        `the calculation row` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the Act the death claim is under`
            WHEN `the Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013` THEN
                `the 2013 Act weekly pension calculation row for` `I am` `with partners` `how many dependent partners the worker left` `children` `how many dependent children are entitled to a pension` `during` `the pension period`
            WHEN `the Accident Compensation Act 1985` THEN
                `the 1985 Act weekly pension calculation row for` `I am` `with partners` `how many dependent partners the worker left` `children` `how many dependent children are entitled to a pension` `during` `the pension period` `claim before 5 April 2010` (`the claim was made before 5 April 2010` `the day the claim was made`)

@export How much will my weekly pension be after the notice's maximum (the amount the Act's formula gives me, or my equal share of the maximum, whichever is less)?
GIVEN `the Act the death claim is under` IS A `Governing Act` @desc Which Act the claim for the worker's death is under
      `the week we ask about` IS A DATE @desc A day in the week for which you want the pension; from 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027
      `the day the claim was made` IS A DATE @desc The day the claim was made; used only for a 1985 Act claim
      `I am` IS A `Dependant kind` @desc Whether you are a dependent partner, or a dependent child (or asking for one)
      `how many dependent partners the worker left` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dependent partners the worker left (0 if none)
      `the dependent children are orphans` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the dependent children are orphans; used only where the worker left no dependent partner
      `how many dependent children are entitled to a pension` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dependent children are entitled to a pension
      `the pension period` IS A `Pension period` @desc Whether the week is during the first 13 weeks, after them but before the end of three years, or after the end of three years
      `the weekly pension the Act's formula gives me` IS A NUMBER @desc Your weekly pension worked out under the Act before any maximum, in Australian dollars; the Act is not deposited, so this is asked
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`my weekly pension after the maximum` `the Act the death claim is under` `the week we ask about` `the day the claim was made` `I am` `how many dependent partners the worker left` `the dependent children are orphans` `how many dependent children are entitled to a pension` `the pension period` `the weekly pension the Act's formula gives me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the most my weekly pension can be` `the Act the death claim is under` `the week we ask about` `the day the claim was made` `I am` `how many dependent partners the worker left` `the dependent children are orphans` `how many dependent children are entitled to a pension` `the pension period`
    WHEN `not covered` `the gap` THEN `not covered` `the gap`
    WHEN `answered` `the figure` THEN `answered` (`the lesser of` `the weekly pension the Act's formula gives me` `and the ceiling` (`the figure`'s `my equal share`))

§§ `Medical and like services for the family (2013 Act s 224(1); 1985 Act s 99(1))`

@export What is the most that can be paid for our family's counselling, therapy and other support services (2013 Act s 224(1)(b); 1985 Act s 99(1)(b))?
GIVEN `the Act the claim is under` IS A `Governing Act` @desc Which Act the worker's claim is under
      `the day we ask about` IS A DATE @desc The day for which you want the amount; from 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`the most our family can be paid for counselling and support` `the Act the claim is under` `the day we ask about` MEANS
    `the figure under` `the Act the claim is under` `on` `the day we ask about` `from` (JUST `the 2013 Act s 224(1)(b) maximum`) `or` (JUST `the 1985 Act s 99(1)(b) maximum`)

@export What is the most I can be paid for travel and accommodation to attend the burial or cremation of the worker (2013 Act s 224(1)(e); 1985 Act s 99(1)(d))?
GIVEN `the Act the death claim is under` IS A `Governing Act` @desc Which Act the claim for the worker's death is under
      `the day we ask about` IS A DATE @desc The day for which you want the amount; from 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027
      `how far the burial or cremation is from my home` IS A NUMBER @desc The distance from your residence to the burial or cremation, in kilometres (the row applies only if it is more than 100 km)
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`the most I can be paid to attend the burial or cremation` `the Act the death claim is under` `the day we ask about` `how far the burial or cremation is from my home` MEANS
    IF `how far the burial or cremation is from my home` GREATER THAN 100
    THEN `the figure under` `the Act the death claim is under` `on` `the day we ask about` `from` (JUST `the 2013 Act s 224(1)(e) maximum`) `or` (JUST `the 1985 Act s 99(1)(d) maximum`)
    ELSE CONSIDER `the notice column in force on` `the day we ask about`
         WHEN `not covered` `the gap` THEN `not covered` `the gap`
         WHEN `answered` `the column` THEN `not covered` `the notice prints this travel and accommodation maximum only where the distance is more than 100 km`

@export What is the most I can be paid for travel and accommodation to be with a severely injured worker in hospital (2013 Act s 224(1)(d))?
GIVEN `the Act the claim is under` IS A `Governing Act` @desc Which Act the worker's claim is under (only the 2013 Act notice prints this row)
      `the day we ask about` IS A DATE @desc The day for which you want the amount; from 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027
      `the worker was severely injured and immediately hospitalised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker was severely injured, as the Act uses the term, and immediately hospitalised following the injury
      `how far my home is from the hospital` IS A NUMBER @desc The distance from your residence to the hospital, in kilometres
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`the most I can be paid to be with the worker in hospital` `the Act the claim is under` `the day we ask about` `the worker was severely injured and immediately hospitalised` `how far my home is from the hospital` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the notice column in force on` `the day we ask about`
    WHEN `not covered` `the gap` THEN `not covered` `the gap`
    WHEN `answered` `the column` THEN
        CONSIDER `the Act the claim is under`
        WHEN `the Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013` THEN `the 2013 Act s 224(1)(d) maximum where severely injured and hospitalised` `the worker was severely injured and immediately hospitalised` `at` `how far my home is from the hospital` `in` `the column`
        WHEN `the Accident Compensation Act 1985` THEN `not covered` `the notice prints no row for this under the Act named`

§§ `Damages for the death (2013 Act s 366(2); 1985 Act s 135C(2)) -- if damages are claimed`

@export What amount does the notice set for damages under Part III of the Wrongs Act 1958 for the death of the worker (2013 Act s 366(2); 1985 Act s 135C(2))?
GIVEN `the Act the death claim is under` IS A `Governing Act` @desc Which Act the claim for the worker's death is under
      `the day we ask about` IS A DATE @desc The day for which you want the amount; from 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`the Wrongs Act damages amount for the death` `the Act the death claim is under` `the day we ask about` MEANS
    `the figure under` `the Act the death claim is under` `on` `the day we ask about` `from` (JUST `the 2013 Act s 366(2) amount`) `or` (JUST `the 1985 Act s 135C(2) amount`)
